Time Complexity: O(1), all the operations will have constant time complexity.Auxiliary Space: O(1)ConclusionSetting, clearing, and toggling specific bits in a number are fundamental operations that can be efficiently performed using bitwise operators in C. These operations are often used in low-level programming, where direct manipulation of individual bits is required, such as in embedded systems, memory management, and cryptography.
